<description>&lt;p&gt;Iraqi authorities are disarming PKK-linked Yazidi militias, including YBŞ and YJŞ, and integrating them into the army and interior ministry while pledging to protect Yazidi rights and Mount Shengal. The intelligence chief Hamid al-Shatri was removed, a court ordered the arrest of the Maysan provincial council chief for defying Iran’s border closure, and parliament approved most remaining cabinet posts, some held by Iran-backed militia figures. A vessel caught fire off Iraq’s Al-Faw coast and Iraqi forces seized more than two tons of drugs in 2026. The conflict produced 396 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMif0FVX3lxTE1QNGxvOEJid2FpVWk0V2lVNnZqV2V0bi11UEtHTTdUSFQ1cE5WQ3VzNjVOVVVLa2puMXVDd0oyRkpKVVIzS3Y1SFdpV29Pa2R2blJlc2lEbjZ4V1hjR01GNGN3MWFSRVE1WGVZSnBmXzhnbGNnNnlIWGNEbjAzZGM?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Jerusalem Post&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiigFBVV95cUxNVnZCT1lKdFFjdGM0RFZWVkpZSXpja0E3cnpQcmJWMWJRYm83QzRydktoLXdKdTZKY0lBUnJnVmxudGdvUFJJZ3VVOXJ6aXRtRThINFY5OXZEYk5KV1JkWk80YW4tNW55elJWaW5vS0gxS1VsWS04NjJmSXc1cU8xVUpYLVlzdHdLM2c?oc=5&quot;&gt;Mirage News&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;GOV.UK&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMirwFBVV95cUxOWUg4RkxFVFdVOFN3SWdDV2RFMGttMWV1MHh3NW5QeUIwcUVrZnJqS0hWdGJXSjRFcExLdE5DdUFReHFVdGtqTlFYT1FxMVowS2ZmUVhTZURyc25nWWFHanpZTGNtWTlDRWJrckFzaHRvbzd2SUJ6Si1nYUdSSGVMRWVmUzh0YnhVaWtJWl9adVE2NDdjWlJwMmJRYkpHbmw0RE96NE84a1RHdjNaVWVZ?oc=5&quot;&gt;United States Mission to the United Nations (.gov)&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiowFBVV95cUxPM1YteEdZdy1yWFNlWXFhaW0zQlE1VDZRc2ZFVThRTHpTQXI4TWJyM3RjT2dhNGpTenVxMGU3aGxwR3hOcDNCM2lsRWRxQlZ6U0xNMUdETkt3d1p2VE85Mkx3QjNiVEJVOGNYTk1NM2w